I want to find out something

00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:11.430
about Reddit or Stack
Overflow or Hacker

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:16.220
News or any other site
that looks interesting,

00:12:16.220 --> 00:12:19.470
if I have to start
by scraping, I just

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:23.470
need to have a lot of energy
to finish that break first.

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:25.050
That's before.

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:30.360
Now I just need to know
that that data is available

00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:31.676
somewhere.

00:12:31.676 --> 00:12:33.000
It's ready on BigQuery.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:36.610
I can just connect and start
asking questions right away.

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:42.795
And I think that's
how Reddit awareness

00:12:42.795 --> 00:12:44.640
that BigQuery existed.

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:49.410
Basically there was this guy
Jason Baumgartner in Washington

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:53.400
that started scraping
every Reddit comment.

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:55.670
Finally, he started
sharing that data.

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:58.280
That data ended up in BigQuery.

00:12:58.280 --> 00:13:02.995
And then one day Reddit itself
sees that that data is there

00:13:02.995 --> 00:13:04.620
and it starts with
writing some queries

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:07.860
without any other effort
other than the data is already

00:13:07.860 --> 00:13:09.120
there for you.

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:12.070
And so it's useful,
it's insightful, it's--

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:16.550
I didn't have to
prepare anything

00:13:16.550 --> 00:13:19.802
to be able to analyze it.

00:13:19.802 --> 00:13:21.720
ANDREI SAVU: Cool.

00:13:21.720 --> 00:13:23.670
So let's talk a little
bit about workloads.

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:26.450
The type of workloads that
this technology powers.

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:31.400
Just to get some examples on
where does the end value come

00:13:31.400 --> 00:13:35.690
from, and kind of like
in terms of the data that

00:13:35.690 --> 00:13:37.750
flows through the
system, what's that data?

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.760
What does it represent for you?

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:45.110
And for Felipe it's more on,
like, interesting examples.

00:13:45.110 --> 00:13:48.020
Like you showed an
example with taxis.

00:13:48.020 --> 00:13:49.740
What else have you
seen that's more,

00:13:49.740 --> 00:13:52.264
like, transformative in nature?

00:13:52.264 --> 00:13:53.930
FELIPE HOFFA: Let me
