00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:13.820
into there, so getting HE proxy
logs parsed into BigQuery,

00:14:13.820 --> 00:14:16.910
so we can see by service
what the availability is.

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:18.170
A lot of business metrics.

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:19.190
OKRs that we track.

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:20.870
Time on site.

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:23.242
You know, DAUs, all
that kind of stuff.

00:14:23.242 --> 00:14:25.700
Some of the more-- and then
there's some interesting, like,

00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:26.510
investigations.

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:28.730
If you look at things
like anti-evil [INAUDIBLE]

00:14:28.730 --> 00:14:32.804
around spam [INAUDIBLE] botnet
detection, vote manipulation.

00:14:32.804 --> 00:14:34.220
There's a lot of
information there

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:38.600
that the difference in
that kind of workflow

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:40.260
is that it's very ad hoc.

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:44.330
So if you had a way that
you could automatically

00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:47.810
detect bots or vote manipulation
that was 100% accurate,

00:14:47.810 --> 00:14:49.970
you would just productize
it and then block them.

00:14:49.970 --> 00:14:51.500
Which we do, but
it's an arms race,

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:52.624
so then they change things.

00:14:52.624 --> 00:14:54.440
So you need a much
more ad-hoc flow

00:14:54.440 --> 00:14:57.860
where we start seeing some
weird behavior on the site

00:14:57.860 --> 00:14:59.630
and you just have
to dig into the data

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:02.130
and pivot it a number of ways
and try to figure out, OK,

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:02.960
what are the common themes?

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:03.980
What are the common threads?

00:15:03.980 --> 00:15:04.980
Is it actually a botnet?

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:05.930
Is it a sleeper cell?

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:08.720
Are there different things
that people are doing here?

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:11.620
And that really helps kind of
that ad hoc [INAUDIBLE] type

00:15:11.620 --> 00:15:12.120
of queries.

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:14.350
So it's been super
helpful there,

00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:17.150
where every 200
iterations on Hive

00:15:17.150 --> 00:15:19.190
would take a couple of
minutes, where, you know,

00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:21.260
if you're doing it just
on a small time range

00:15:21.260 --> 00:15:24.080
it takes a couple of seconds
to get an answer for looking

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:26.120
at enough data where
you-- like, things where

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:27.245
you need aggregates, right?

00:15:27.245 --> 00:15:29.510
Like to know if I have a
vote manipulation or botnet,

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:31.132
I can't look at, like 100 votes.

00:15:31.132 --> 00:15:32.590
I have to look at
millions of votes

00:15:32.590 --> 00:15:35.090
and start seeing what
the patterns are.

00:15:35.090 --> 00:15:36.680
So that's been
super helpful there.

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:38.930
So essentially right
now, business metrics,

00:15:38.930 --> 00:15:42.020
KPIs, understanding how
people are using the site, how

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:43.580
the site is behaving.

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:45.800
And then as well as
ad hoc investigations

00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:49.460
on different things around
the anti-evil space.

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:51.980
There's a couple of
interesting things with Bill.

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:53.750
I have one query that
actually gives me

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:56.150
a listing, like same
thing as you see when you

00:15:56.150 --> 00:15:57.950
